  "body": "• Solid 1970s brick home, renovated inside and out \r\n• 809sqm freehold site (more or less), zoned Mixed Housing Suburban\r\n• Elevated position capturing beautiful urban and sea views\r\n• Three sun-filled bedrooms upstairs, with a sea glimpse from two bedrooms\r\n• Flexible downstairs bedroom, bathroom and living area with independent access\r\n• Northwest-facing, fully fenced, established garden with mature fruit trees and room for children and dogs to play \r\n• Potential to explore an extension, additional outdoor living spaces, or even a minor dwelling (subject to council approval).\r\n• Double internal-access garage and ample off-street parking for additional vehicles, a boat or caravan\r\n• Zoned for Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College\r\n• Kindergartens and primary schools just moments away\r\n• Close to Torbay Village, public transport, beaches and reserves\r\n• Vendors are committed to moving overseas, this property must be sold\r\n\r\nPositioned on an elevated 809sqm freehold site (more or less), this solid 1970s brick home has been renovated inside and out. Thoughtfully transformed for modern living, it combines fresh contemporary interiors with the character of its original era.\r\n\r\nElevated above the bays, this beautifully renovated family home captures sweeping sea and urban views, creating an impressive backdrop to everyday life. Here, contemporary comfort meets the space and freedom of a traditional Kiwi family property, with room to breathe and possibilities for the future.\r\n\r\nThe upper level centres around light-filled livings and dining spaces, where expansive glazing frames the outlook. Easy flow to the deck creates the perfect setting to relax and entertain, while the brand-new contemporary kitchen offers a practical layout and quality appliances.\r\n\r\nFeaturing four bedrooms, 2.5 bathrooms and two living areas, the versatile layout provides plenty of space for the whole family. Three sun-filled bedrooms are located upstairs, with a sea glimpse from two north facing sunny bedrooms and an established garden outlook from the 3rd bedroom.\r\n\r\nThe lower level offers a separate living area, fourth bedroom and bathroom, together with independent access. This flexible space is ideal as a teenager's retreat or accommodation for extended family and guests. A potential income opportunity could also be explored, subject to any required approvals.\r\n\r\nOutside, the mature, northwest-facing garden is a hidden treasure. Fully fenced, with established fruit trees and generous outdoor spaces, it offers room for children and dogs to play, family and friends to gather, and keen gardeners to create their dream garden. Whether you envision a vegetable patch, colourful flower beds or a peaceful retreat among the greenery, there is space to make it your own.\r\n\r\nThe generous grounds also invite ideas for the future. Explore additional decking or outdoor entertaining areas, or the possibility of extending the home or adding a minor dwelling towards the rear of the site. All options are subject to site feasibility and any necessary council approvals, offering scope for buyers with vision.\r\n\r\nParking is equally generous, with a double internal-access garage and ample off-street space for additional vehicles, a boat or caravan.\r\n\r\nFor land-bankers, the Mixed Housing Suburban zoning may offer further redevelopment potential, subject to council approval.\r\n\r\nSet among quality homes, the location is exceptionally convenient for families. Local kindergartens and primary schools are just moments away, with zoning for Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College. Torbay Village, public transport, beautiful beaches and reserves are within easy reach, while nearby Albany offers extensive shopping, dining and entertainment options, along with motorway connections.\r\n\r\nWith their overseas move firmly planned, our vendors are committed to selling. Discover a renovated family home with room to grow, space to enjoy and potential to make your own.\r\n\r\nConjunctional enquiries are welcome from day one.",
